  "meta": {
    "audit_log": {
      "deletion": "immutable",
      "append_only": true,
      "note": "APPEND-ONLY (SEC-6): who (actor_id, actor_roles), what (action, entity, entity_id), before/after JSON text, reason, ip, request_id, occurred_at (UTC). Read: opsadmin and safeguardinglead via per-row read grants written by the core service (no table-level label read). No client write permission. INTENDED insert-only via AppendOnlyRepository (opt-in, not wired yet: nothing uses it; see appwrite/README.md). Index prefix for lookups: (entity, entity_id, occurred_at); actor_id is NULL for system actions. before/after are text (about 16k chars): the core service must summarise or truncate larger diffs (M06 #41 / $01 follow-up).",
      "non_fk": {
        "entity_id": "polymorphic reference to any audited row, discriminated by entity",
        "request_id": "correlation id of the HTTP request, not a row id"
      }
    },
    "notification_template": {
      "deletion": "immutable",
      "note": "Central templates with variables per channel (SR 8, N01 #126 builds the service on this table). Editing = new version row (unique key+channel+locale+version), so sent notifications keep the exact version. allowed_variables lists the placeholders a body may use (missing variable blocks the send, N01). Super admin edits through the core service."
    },
    "notification": {
      "deletion": "soft",
      "note": "One row per send with delivery status (SR 5.1/8). category operational and safeguarding cannot be muted; marketing can (N01). dedupe_key unique so a retried job does not send twice. Push failures for critical events fall back to email (status fallback). Rows are kept until retention. Quiet hours for non-urgent push (SR 8, e.g. 21:00-07:00 Kampala) are a global setting, not per-user (no column here) unless the owner says otherwise; N01 #126 follow-up."
    },
    "notification_preference": {
      "deletion": "hard",
      "note": "Marketing mute only (SR 8). The one user-writable table in ADR 0012 item 2 (update(user:<id>) on the row, set by the core service when it creates the row). Never soft-deleted (a soft delete would either hide a financial/idempotency record or free its unique value): the lifecycle is the status column; only the retention job hard-deletes it, after the retention period (DP-6, SR 5.5). One row per user (unique user_id); removed with the user under retention."
    },
    "device_token": {
      "deletion": "history",
      "note": "FCM tokens per user and app; revoked_at on logout or invalid token, row kept for history until retention. The token is a sensitive bearer-style secret: never logged (F08 scrubber), never listed to admins, rows carry per-row read/none permissions only (the core service reads them; no table-level or label permission). token_hash = sha256 hex of the token, unique: lookups by token on rotation or invalid-token feedback use the hash; Upsert rule: register = look up by token_hash. If no row, insert. If a row exists for the same user (re-register after revoke), clear revoked_at and set last_seen_at. If the token arrives for a different user (shared device), update user_id to the new user, rewrite the row's read permission to that user, clear revoked_at and set last_seen_at: never keep two live rows for one token. Revoke on logout."
    }
  },
